What you need to do

- Locally: nothing. I already applied the migration to your running local Supabase, so just use the app.
- On a hosted Supabase project (when you deploy):
  a. Install and log in to the CLI: supabase login.
  b. From backend, run supabase link --project-ref <your-project-ref>. You'll find the ref in the dashboard URL.
  c. Run supabase db push to create the bucket and policies. Or open Dashboard → SQL Editor and paste in the contents of the migration file.
  d. Check Dashboard → Storage: log-photos should be listed as Public.
  e. Set VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in frontend/.env to the hosted project's values. Don't put the service role key in the frontend.

Limits

- Each log holds one photo. You said "pics", so if you want several per log I can add up to 3, but that needs a small database change.
- Photos are public to anyone who has the link. They aren't listed anywhere, but if you'd rather keep them private I can switch to signed URLs.
